"language": "eng"
}
]
}
},
{
"content_id": "132934",
"reference_id": 108988,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Colossians 3:18–4:1",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "51003018-51004001",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "None",
"content": "<p>Earlier Paul gave instructions about how believers were to live together in <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"131991\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">God’s family</data>. They were to put on tender <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132288\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">mercy</data> and kindness as if they were clothes.</p><p>Paul showed how they were to do this within their human families as well. His instructions were different from what was common in <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"131993\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">Roman</data> lands in his time. It was common for women, children and <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132204\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">slaves</data> to be taught to obey. Yet Paul taught believers to base their relationships on serving Jesus.</p><p>Everyone was to follow Jesus’ example of being a <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132005\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">leader who serves</data>. Paul taught husbands to show love. He taught fathers to show kindness. He taught masters to be humble and fair. And he reminded all believers that they are slaves of the Lord Jesus. Jesus is the Master they must all obey.</p>",
"associations": {
"passage": [
{
"start_ref": "51003018",
"start_ref_usfm": "COL 3:18",
"end_ref": "51004001",
"end_ref_usfm": "COL 4:1"
}
],
